    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d373-a2">

                <pb facs="0489" n="401" xml:id="pg401"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr. Férère.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-09-02"><hi rendition="#italic">September 2,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your excellency’s favor, in which you call my attention to the naturalization
                    of a certain class of persons who claim to be American citizens.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to state to your excellency that this legation has been for some
                    time engaged on this matter, and that it is awaiting further instructions from
                    the honorable Secretary of State, Hon. John Hay, in regard to it.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
